  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "Ben wanted to join the drama club, but he did not enjoy speaking on stage.",
      "He thought every club member had to act.",
      "When he saw the sign for new members, he nearly walked past."
    ],
    [
      "The club leader explained that each show would involve more than actors.",
      "Someone needed to organise the equipment, check the music and help with the lights.",
      "Ben enjoyed planning, so these jobs sounded suitable for him."
    ],
    [
      "At the first meeting, everyone wrote down their personal interests.",
      "The leader did not use the list to put people into permanent roles.",
      "Instead, members could try a job and discuss whether it suited them."
    ],
    [
      "Ben began by checking the equipment list.",
      "Later, he offered to read one short line during a practice.",
      "The club had given him a comfortable place to start, not a rule that he must stay behind the stage.",
      "Good organisation helped people join in while leaving room for their interests to change."
    ]
  ],
  "translations": [
    "本想参加戏剧社，但不喜欢站在舞台上讲话。",
    "他以为每个社员都必须演戏。",
    "看到招募新成员的告示时，他差一点直接走过去。",
    "社长解释说，每场演出需要参与的人不只是演员。",
    "还需要有人整理器材、检查音乐，并协助灯光工作。",
    "本喜欢做计划，所以这些工作听起来很适合他。",
    "第一次开会时，每个人都写下自己的兴趣。",
    "社长并没有用这张清单把大家固定在某些角色上。",
    "相反，社员可以先尝试一种工作，再讨论是否适合自己。",
    "本一开始负责核对器材清单。",
    "后来，他主动提出在一次练习中念一句短台词。",
    "社团给了他一个舒适的起点，而不是规定他必须一直待在幕后。",
    "良好的组织安排帮助大家参与，也为兴趣的变化留下了空间。"
  ],
